phie was referring to now  if i had to guess i would say the scene  she filmed with ramsay on their wedding  night had to be one of the hardest  scenes to be in  filming something like that especially  at such a young age must have affected  her in some way  obviously i'm not the one who should be  discussing something like this so i will  move on to the next thing that was  mentioned during the interview  maisie was also asked if she still talks  to anyone she worked with on the show  she said everyone we're all on a group  chat which is lovely everyone's doing  really well and i think that it's nice  to keep up with them while they're  enjoying their lives which had been  dominated by the show for so long  now that is certainly nice to hear i  like knowing that they're all still  friends even now three years after the  show has ended i don't know about all of  you but i still get excited whenever i  see someone from game of thrones in a  new show or movie i'm about to watch  alright now this is when they ask her if  she will be watching house of the dragon  maisie said yes i'm really looking  forward to it actually my friend olivia  who we all know as allison hightower is  in the show and it's been really  interesting just chatting to her about  the experience i think it's actually a  lot more pressure for them all of the  hungover concerns of our show are now  just being thrown onto this new cast who  had nothing to do with it i want to be  as supportive as i can to her as an  actress but also i'm just really curious  i'm kind of looking forward to watching  game of thrones even though it's not  actually game of thrones i want to  experience it as someone that's not on  it all i've done is meet fans who have  done just that and i never really was  able to relate to it well maisy is  definitely right about one thing old  fans of game of thrones are worried that  the same mistakes will be made on house  of the dragon which isn't entirely fair  considering dan and dave no longer work  for hbo this is a new show with new  writers that already has an amazing  ending written by george rr martin in  another recent interview maisie said she  would consider stepping back into the  role as arya stark someday and that made  a lot of news the interviewer wanted to  know if that news did surprise her  maisie said no are you kidding me i  haven't given anyone anything else to  talk about yet that's what everyone  wants from me but they're not gonna get  it until the time is right  it's nice to know what they want from  you even if it's not what you're ready  to give  now maybe i am wrong about this but it  does seem like maisy would be arya stark  again i bet a lot of the old game of  thrones actors would step back into  westeros again for most of them it will  be the most successful thing they will  ever work on now i'm sure by the end of  season 8 some of them did want a break  from the show but now that we're three  years separated from the ending some of  them would most likely jump at the  chance at joining hbo again for another  incredible run  now what they discuss next is how maisie  williams is very selective about what  she says during her interviews  especially whenever game of thrones is  mentioned  in fact maisie actually admits that she  does do this which we all knew already  almost everyone does this whenever  they're giving an interview now what  they ask her after this is why she does  that what is she worried about saying  regarding game of thrones  they say it seems like maybe you don't  want to be the center of a negative  story about the show given how everyone  talked about it at the very end  obviously there was a lot of negative  feedback after the final season aired  maisie said no i don't want to defend  the show for that reason i don't really  i don't really mind that it ended that  way  we were so disconnected from i felt like  my life and how it changed was so  disconnected from the actual storyline  of the 